# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA) is a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm designed to solve combinatorial optimization problems such as max-cut and general QUBO formulations. For a foundational introduction to QAOA in Qiskit, see the [QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm); for more advanced circuit-building techniques, see the [advanced QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa).\n"
msgstr "Ang Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA) ay isang hybrid quantum-classical algorithm na idinisenyo para lutasin ang mga combinatorial optimization problem tulad ng max-cut at pangkalahatang QUBO formulations. Para sa pundasyunal na panimula sa QAOA sa Qiskit, tingnan ang [QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm); para sa mas advanced na circuit-building techniques, tingnan ang [advanced QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In standard QAOA:\n"
"- The initial state is the uniform superposition $|+\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"- Variational parameters are randomly initialized.\n"
"- A classical optimizer searches for parameters that minimize the cost function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa standard QAOA:\n"
"- Ang initial state ay ang uniform superposition $|+\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"- Random na na-initialize ang variational parameters.\n"
"- Ang classical optimizer ay naghahanap ng mga parameter na nagpapaliit sa cost function.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, for practical problem sizes and noisy quantum hardware, random initialization can lead to slow convergence, poor local minima, and increased optimization cost.\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, para sa praktikal na laki ng problema at maingay (noisy) na quantum hardware, ang random initialization ay maaaring magresulta sa mabagal na convergence, mahihinang local minima, at pagtaas ng optimization cost.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Warm-start QAOA** (WS-QAOA) improves this by incorporating classical optimization insights directly into the quantum circuit. This tutorial follows the methods introduced by Egger, Mareček, and Woerner in [*Warm-starting quantum optimization*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.10095). The key idea is to:\n"
msgstr "Pinapabuti ito ng **Warm-start QAOA** (WS-QAOA) sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama ng mga insight mula sa classical optimization nang direkta sa quantum circuit. Sinusunod ng tutorial na ito ang mga metodo na ipinakilala nina Egger, Mareček, at Woerner sa [*Warm-starting quantum optimization*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.10095). Ang pangunahing ideya ay:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Solve a continuous relaxation** of the original binary problem (a quadratic program over $[0,1]^n$ instead of $\\{0,1\\}^n$).\n"
msgstr "**Lutasin ang continuous relaxation** ng orihinal na binary problem (isang quadratic program sa $[0,1]^n$ sa halip na $\\{0,1\\}^n$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Encode the relaxed solution** $c^*_i \\in [0,1]$ into a custom initial state by using $Y$-rotation angles $\\theta_i = 2\\arcsin(\\sqrt{c^*_i})$, so that qubit $i$ starts in a state whose probability of measuring $|1\\rangle$ is $c^*_i$.\n"
msgstr "**I-encode ang relaxed solution** $c^*_i \\in [0,1]$ patungo sa custom initial state gamit ang $Y$-rotation angles $\\theta_i = 2\\arcsin(\\sqrt{c^*_i})$, para ang qubit $i$ ay magsisimula sa isang state kung saan ang probability ng pagsukat ng $|1\\rangle$ ay $c^*_i$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Replace the standard $X$-mixer** with a custom mixer whose ground state is the warm-start initial state, ensuring the algorithm starts near the classical solution and can explore the neighborhood.\n"
msgstr "**Palitan ang standard $X$-mixer** ng custom mixer na ang ground state ay ang warm-start initial state, tinitiyak na ang algorithm ay nagsisimula malapit sa classical solution at kayang tuklasin ang paligid nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A regularization parameter $\\varepsilon \\in [0, 0.5]$ clips $c^*_i$ away from 0 and 1 to avoid reachability issues; qubits initialized in $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ cannot be moved by the cost Hamiltonian. At $\\varepsilon = 0.5$, WS-QAOA reduces exactly to standard QAOA.\n"
msgstr "Isang regularization parameter na $\\varepsilon \\in [0, 0.5]$ ay nagki-clip sa $c^*_i$ palayo sa 0 at 1 para maiwasan ang reachability issues; ang mga qubit na na-initialize sa $|0\\rangle$ o $|1\\rangle$ ay hindi maaaring galawin ng cost Hamiltonian. Sa $\\varepsilon = 0.5$, ang WS-QAOA ay eksaktong nababawas patungo sa standard QAOA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Problem modeling uses the [`qiskit-addon-opt-mapper`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/) package, whose [`Maxcut`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/stubs/qiskit_addon_opt_mapper.applications.Maxcut.html) application class builds the QUBO directly from a graph, and whose converters and translators map the resulting problem to quantum Hamiltonians.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng problem modeling ang [`qiskit-addon-opt-mapper`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/) package, na ang [`Maxcut`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/stubs/qiskit_addon_opt_mapper.applications.Maxcut.html) application class ay bumubuo ng QUBO nang direkta mula sa graph, at ang mga converter at translator nito ay nagma-map sa nagresultang problema patungo sa quantum Hamiltonians.\n"

